<https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ccore#isQualityOf> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ccore#Impact> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The consequences of realized risks on natural and human systems, where risks result from the interactions of climate-related hazards (including extreme weather/climate events), exposure, and vulnerability. Impacts generally refer to effects on lives, livelihoods, health and well-being, ecosystems and species, economic, social and cultural assets, services (including ecosystem services), and infrastructure. Impacts may be referred to as consequences or outcomes and can be adverse or beneficial. See also Adaptation, Exposure, Hazard, Vulnerability and Risk." .
<https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ccore#ElementAtRisk> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "We say that an element is 'at risk' with respect to a certain threat perdurant if it is a service or a physical endurant for which an impact has been documented that results from the same threat perdurant and impacts on that element." .
<https://w3id.org/crima-ontology/ccore#proxyContent> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
